year": -1150, "title": "Deir Alla falls", "text": "The Jordan valley sanctuary, which held a vessel naming Egypt's Queen Tawosret, is destroyed about now.", "lon": -54.111, "lat": -9.502}, {"year": -1150, "title": "Philistine Ashdod", "text": "Ashdod is a Philistine city, with Aegean-style pottery made on the spot.", "lon": -56.421, "lat": -10.759}, {"year": -1150, "title": "Ekron grows", "text": "The Philistine city at Tel Miqne expands into a walled, planned town.", "lon": -55.964, "lat": -10.675}, {"year": -1148, "title": "Hala Sultan Tekke abandoned", "text": "A rich harbour town of Cyprus is deserted around the middle of the century.", "lon": -58.948, "lat": -2.017}, {"year": -1145, "title": "Timna abandoned", "text": "The last royal name at the Hathor shrine of the copper mines is Ramesses V.", "lon": -55.7, "lat": -16.233}, {"year": -1140, "title": "Statue at Megiddo", "text": "A bronze statue base of Ramesses VI, the latest royal sign of Egypt at Megiddo.", "lon": -55.17, "lat": -8.441}, {"year": -1138, "title": "Sinai turquoise ends", "text": "Ramesses VI is the last king named at the turquoise mines of Serabit el-Khadim.", "lon": -59.309, "lat": -18.328}, {"year": -1136, "title": "Ramesses VI buried", "text": "The king is buried in the Valley of the Kings, in a tomb begun for Ramesses V.", "lon": -61.379, "lat": -27.544}, {"year": -1135, "title": "Jaffa gate burns", "text": "Fire destroys the gate of Egypt's garrison at Jaffa; it is rebuilt.", "lon": -56.205, "lat": -9.921}, {"year": -1130, "title": "Megiddo destroyed", "text": "The Canaanite city at Megiddo burns about now; who did it is unknown.", "lon": -55.122, "lat": -8.385}, {"year": -1130, "title": "Lachish destroyed", "text": "The city at Lachish, which held an object naming Ramesses III, burns and lies empty.", "lon": -55.964, "lat": -11.29}, {"year": -1130, "title": "Deir el-Balah ends", "text": "Burials in clay coffins at the Egyptian outpost south of Gaza come to an end during the century.", "lon": -57.24, "lat": -11.681}, {"year": -1125, "title": "Jaffa's last fire", "text": "The rebuilt gate burns again; radiocarbon on charred seeds points to about 1125 BC.", "lon": -56.157, "lat": -9.977}, {"year": -1120, "title": "Beth Shean lingers", "text": "Some scholars see Egyptians at this inland base into the next century.", "lon": -54.4, "lat": -8.664}, {"year": -1116, "title": "Amenhotep's relief", "text": "At Karnak the high priest has himself carved as large as Ramesses IX.", "lon": -61.234, "lat": -27.6}, {"year": -1115, "title": "Libyans near Thebes", "text": "Tomb workers of Deir el-Medina stop work for fear of Libyan raiders.", "lon": -61.379, "lat": -27.572}, {"year": -1110, "title": "Tomb robbery inquiry", "text": "Officials inspect the royal tombs; suspects are beaten to extract confessions.", "lon": -61.427, "lat": -27.488}, {"year": -1110, "title": "Dor's stone quays", "text": "Dor builds sea walls and quays, its culture closest to the Phoenician coast.", "lon": -55.796, "lat": -8.329}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Tiglath-Pileser in Lebanon", "text": "The Assyrian king cuts cedar on Mount Lebanon for his temples.", "lon": -53.077, "lat": -3.805}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Payments from Phoenicia", "text": "Byblos, Sidon and Arwad pay the Assyrian king.", "lon": -54.039, "lat": -4.14}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Sailing from Arwad", "text": "Tiglath-Pileser takes ship from the island of Arwad along the coast of Amurru.", "lon": -53.534, "lat": -2.073}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Aramean wars", "text": "Assyria fights Aramean tribes along the Euphrates and around Jebel Bishri.", "lon": -45.496, "lat": -0.844}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Faynan copper", "text": "Copper smelting expands in the Faynan valley of Transjordan.", "lon": -54.617, "lat": -13.887}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Enkomi declines", "text": "Cyprus's great copper town slowly shrinks.", "lon": -58.25, "lat": -1.235}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Tell Qasile", "text": "A Philistine harbour town stands on the Yarkon river by about this time.", "lon": -56.085, "lat": -9.781}, {"year": -1100, "title": "Tyre on its island", "text": "Tyre trades from its island site; its great age is still to come.", "lon": -55.122, "lat": -6.514}, {"year": -1099, "title": "Ramesses XI crowned", "text": "The last Ramesses takes the throne, ruling from the Delta capital of Pi-Ramesses.", "lon": -63.232, "lat": -13.412}, {"year": -1090, "title": "Libyan forts", "text": "Libyan families hold garrison towns around Herakleopolis; later pharaohs descend from them.", "lon": -65.397, "lat": -18.216}, {"year": -1087, "title": "Panehsy at Thebes", "text": "The viceroy of Kush and his Nubian troops are in Thebes, managing its grain.", "lon": -61.258, "lat": -27.684}, {"year": -1082, "title": "War on the priest", "text": "Panehsy moves against the high priest Amenhotep, who appeals to the king.", "lon": -61.379, "lat": -27.6}, {"year": -1081, "title": "Hardai sacked", "text": "War reaches Middle Egypt, and Panehsy's forces plunder the town of Hardai.", "lon": -65.734, "lat": -19.892}, {"year": -1080, "title": "Repeating of Births", "text": "A new era is proclaimed in year 19 of Ramesses XI, and power is divided.", "lon": -61.234, "lat": -27.6}, {"year": -1080, "title": "Panehsy in Nubia", "text": "Driven south, Panehsy holds on in Nubia, beyond the reach of Thebes.", "lon": -60.681, "lat": -32.152}, {"year": -1078, "title": "Herihor at Karnak", "text": "The high priest and general appears in royal style on the Khonsu temple, with Amun's barque.", "lon": -61.234, "lat": -27.628}, {"year": -1078, "title": "Smendes at Tanis", "text": "Smendes rules the Delta from Tanis, with Ramesses XI still nominally king.", "lon": -63.111, "lat": -12.937}, {"year": -1075, "title": "Wenamun sets out", "text": "Wenamun leaves Thebes for Lebanon's cedar, by the traditional date.", "lon": -61.282, "lat": -27.656}, {"year": -1075, "title": "Robbed at Dor", "text": "A crewman flees with five deben of gold and thirty-one of silver; Prince Beder refuses to pay.", "lon": -55.82, "lat": -8.329}, {"year": -1075, "title": "Twenty-nine days", "text": "At Byblos, Prince Zakar-Baal orders Wenamun out of the harbour every day.", "lon": -54.063, "lat": -4.14}, {"year": -1074, "title": "Eleven Tjeker ships", "text": "Ships arrive at Byblos to arrest Wenamun as the logs lie ready on the shore.", "lon": -54.111, "lat": -4.084}, {"year": -1074, "title": "Saved by Hatiba", "text": "A storm carries Wenamun to Alashiya; a princess stops a mob, and the papyrus breaks off.", "lon": -58.9, "lat": -1.906}, {"year": -1072, "title": "Medinet Habu refuge", "text": "Tomb workers move within the walls of the temple at Medinet Habu for safety.", "lon": -61.379, "lat": -27.6}, {"year": -1071, "title": "Piankh in Nubia", "text": "The general Piankh leads an army south to meet Panehsy, and writes home ordering an old tomb opened.", "lon": -60.777, "lat": -32.264}, {"year": -1069, "title": "Ramesses XI dies", "text": "The New Kingdom ends: Smendes becomes king at Tanis, and priests rule Thebes.", "lon": -63.111, "lat": -12.993}], "eras": [[-1150, -1136, "The Last Garrisons"], [-1135, -1125, "The Fall of the Forts"], [-1124, -1100, "The New Coast"], [-1099, -1081, "The Theban Crisis"], [-1080, -1069, "The Repeating of Births"]], "refLine": null, "metrics": [{"label": "Under one pharaoh", "stages": [1, 4]}, {"label": "Sea Peoples and Phoenicians", "stages": [2, 3]}], "chartNote": "Share of the area of today's countries, by who held the upper hand there. This is a simplification: regions are today's boundaries, one colour stands for a whole country, and Egypt's deserts dominate the shares. Egypt cannot be split on this map, so its 'Libyan or Theban power base' colour covers a land divided between Thebes and Tanis. Egyptian dates follow Kitchen's chronology and are approximate; the end of Egyptian rule in Canaan is debated. Wenamun's voyage is placed at its traditional date, and the report itself may be lit